WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.330
<i>That day, that time...</i>

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.750
<i>We were thrown into the future,
into the year 2388.</i>

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.470
<i>We continued to struggle
without a way to return to our time.</i>

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.760
<i>We fought off the all-out attack
by the Revisions, but...</i>

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.430
<i>Milo wasn't there.</i>

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.770
<i>To complete the AHRV mission,</i>

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.900
<i>she went to find us in 2010.</i>

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.650
<i>Mr. Kuroiwa and then Milo...</i>

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.650
<i>The people we depended on are gone.</i>

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.490
<i>Then our only means of resistance,</i>

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.580
<i>the String Puppets,
almost ran out of power.</i>

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:46.670
<i>But even after all that,
a tiny light appeared within me.</i>

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.550
You know, that weird dark machine...

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.130
I'm sure that was Keisaku.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:02.140
So I'm wondering if there could be
some way to bring him back.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.810
Milo is gone now.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.560
She leaped back in time

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.440
to protect us.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.960
<i>Slowly.</i>

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.300
It's a lot lighter than it looks.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.510
That was a big help.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.340
Thank you very much for helping us out.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.720
No problem.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.220
If you need anything else, let us know.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.680
Those people are doing their best
along with Ms. Yumiko.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.980
Yes, you're right.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.030
About what you just said...

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.070
What do you think?

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.530
I'm certain that was Keisaku.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:24.030
But Milo said that since
Keisaku doesn't have a quantum brain,

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.490
he can't go anywhere.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.450
<i>But that dark thing saved Marimari.</i>

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.660
<i>Right, Marimari?</i>

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.130
<i>Yes, but...</i>

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.540
<i>I'm telling you. I'm sure of it.</i>

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.710
<i>We have to do something
to help Keisaku return to normal.</i>

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.760
<i>-Right, Gai?
-How?</i>

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.510
<i>Well, if we all talk to him...</i>

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.760
Isn't that dangerous?

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.390
Well, if we use the String Puppets...

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.560
He showed up
when we were using the String Puppets.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.560
But now the String Puppets don't work.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.690
We can't think about saving Keisaku

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.780
when we can't even return to our time
by our own power.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.320
<i>We're terribly sorry!</i>

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:09.490
What are you talking about?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.170
At that time,
we were misled by what Mayor Muta said.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.540
Oh, forget about that.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.460
Right?

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.960
To be honest,
I don't want to see your faces.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:25.010
<i>You're also to blame
for Chief Kuroiwa's death.</i>

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.850
<i>But the Chief's last words were,
"Everyone must return."</i>

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.600
Everyone left here must cooperate.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.150
I'll do my best to put it out of my mind.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.320
Then let's move on to the issue at hand.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.200
<i>At present,
the Revisions' attack has ceased.</i>

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.030
<i>It's not clear
when they will attack again.</i>

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.240
<i>In addition, I heard
that the electricity supplied by the Cube,</i>

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.080
<i>which is our source of power,
is almost used up.</i>

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.210
Yes. Due to that,

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.540
<i>we can't count on
the String Puppets to function.</i>

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.130
<i>You're kidding.</i>

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.130
But what if we get attacked
by the Revisions again?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.840
I think if we redirect
all the power left for the city

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.430
to the String Puppets,

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.850
they can be used
for about two or three hours.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.520
In light of that,

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.270
I'd like to determine what action
we should take as the government.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.810
Let's hear the opinion of everyone.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:18.730
Well...

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:22.030
Could we form a suicide squad
to attack the Revisions' base?

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.240
-It's not that easy!
-Yes, ma'am!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.320
But wasn't the SDS given

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.950
many privileges
for this kind of situation?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.910
They are high schoolers!

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.830
They are ordinary students.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.120
Those kids don't even have proper weapons.
Are you saying we should sacrifice them?

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.670
Well, no...

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.710
May I raise a suggestion?

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.800
Go ahead.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.170
I have two suggestions.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.380
<i>First, as for the RV virus,</i>

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.680
<i>I've gathered
all the necessary documentation on it.</i>

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:53.010
<i>At present,
it's stored at the UN facility.</i>

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.100
If we return to our time,
we can analyze it,

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.980
and maybe we can prevent the pandemic
before it happens.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.400
<i>Next, as for the remaining power...</i>

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.190
<i>I hope you're all okay.</i>

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.610
<i>Were you able to fight off the Revisions?</i>

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:10.410
What is this?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.740
<i>-I'm sorry I had to leave you</i>
-A message Milo left for us.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.240
<i>to leap back in time.</i>

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.080
<i>I will tell you now everything
that I couldn't say before.</i>

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.000
<i>This is what AHRV speculates
about the Revisions' plan.</i>

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.340
<i>Shibuya is part of an experiment</i>

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.050
<i> to transport whole areas
from the past to the future.</i>

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.760
<i>If it succeeds,</i>

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:32.970
<i>they will transport other places
around the world to the future.</i>

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.890
<i>By doing so,
they will bypass the pandemic era</i>

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.600
<i>and avoid the decline of humanity.</i>

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.190
To save humanity?

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:47.740
<i>But AHRV believes that the Revisions are
only saying that it will save humanity,</i>

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.070
<i>but it's nothing more than a way for them
to secure materials for themselves.</i>

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.790
<i>But AHRV saw value
in taking advantage of this plan.</i>

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.660
<i>What will happen if huge numbers of humans
are brought from the past?</i>

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.000
<i>People of the past</i>

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:06.840
<i>will detest the Revisions since
they don't seem human and side with AHRV.</i>

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.550
<i>In fact, you people
from Shibuya reacted that way.</i>

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.970
<i>AHRV believed</i>

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:16.680
<i>that discriminatory feelings based on
appearance would lead to ultimate victory.</i>

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.850
<i>That's why AHRV didn't prevent
the Revisions' plan.</i>

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.900
Despicable.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.770
<i>According to AHRV's prediction,</i>

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.480
<i>the String Puppets would demonstrate
clear military superiority,</i>

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.110
<i>and Shibuya would
safely return to its time.</i>

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.950
<i>However,
an unpredictable problem occurred.</i>

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.870
<i>Keisaku became a time-space singularity.</i>

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.290
<i>Most likely, the dark entity
that keeps appearing in front of Daisuke</i>

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.080
<i>is Keisaku.</i>

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.590
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:49.590
<i>I was ordered to leap back to 2010 to
remove the impediment to our prediction</i>

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.470
<i>and eliminate Keisaku Asano.</i>

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.390
What?

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.430
<i>This leads to the next point.</i>

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.520
<i>AHRV determined that the people
of Shibuya failed,</i>

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.980
<i>didn't return Shibuya to 2017,
and remained here in this time.</i>

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.190
<i>I'm an AHRV...</i>

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.110
-What?
-Did the battery die?

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.110
Eliminate Keisaku? How can--

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.240
Bastards!

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.910
How could they say
that we failed? Goddamn it!

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:15.820
Gai!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.280
Wait! Gai!

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:18.700
Gai.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.580
TWO WEEKS LATER

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.470
Ms. Izumi!

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.930
It's all right!

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:45.350
The SDS and police are fighting
the Revisions now!

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.360
We'll drive them off like always.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:49.940
Don't worry!

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:51.360
They're leaving.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:53.740
It's a success, Ms. Izumi.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.370
<i>They are humans after all.
They are afraid of fire.</i>

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.420
<i>You AHRV tool!</i>

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.170
You tricked us!

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:12.840
Traitor!

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.430
Hey! That's enough.

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.510
Who the hell are you?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.720
You're satisfied now, right?

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.680
You've done enough.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.180
Shut up, you punk!

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.560
You're that kid from back then.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.280
It feels good

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:35.150
to righteously kick the ass of some prick.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:36.820
Hey!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.360
Let's go. Get up.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:41.830
I can't believe we protected
jerks like that.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.330
Gai, wait!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.870
Come back, Gai.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.540
It's too late for that. There's no hope.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.960
But Lu and Marimari are still
doing their best--

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.630
Now that the String Puppets
don't work anymore,

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:59.840
we're just getting blamed
by the people we saved.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.600
Those two have been in danger
several times as well.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.020
Again and again.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:09.230
How can you keep this up?

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.440
Well, this is all I can do.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.730
What's with that?

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:17.490
You used to act like we would find
a way out if we try hard enough.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.450
Is that how you really feel?

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.240
No. They are both how I feel.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:26.290
When I think about it, everyone besides me
was doing what they should.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.920
Gai, Lu, Marimari, and Keisaku too.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.920
I was the only one who wasn't serious.
I shouldn't have acted like that.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.590
This is the least I can do now,
or I'll have nothing.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.260
<i>Where do you want to eat?</i>

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.100
<i>We're going out again today?</i>

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.480
<i>Girls do nothing but eat.</i>

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.520
<i>You'll get fat.</i>

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.850
<i>No, we won't!</i>

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.310
<i>A little extra flesh is kind of nice.</i>

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:53.650
<i>You pervert!</i>

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:12.420
<i>Is it true that the Civilians
have started to assemble again?</i>

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:13.750
Yes.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.420
We're worried that they will come at us
in the numbers they did before.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:18.920
Everyone is frightened.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:20.340
I see.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.550
-Say...
-What?

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.310
Can you get your hands on a car?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.510
A car?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.640
If we're never going back,

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.940
then why don't we return
to the Revisions' base?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.730
-Are you serious?
-Yes.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.320
Do you want to die?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.650
Don't you dare!

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.400
Mikio!

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.700
Don't you dare do anything
as crazy as that.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.910
Gai, I've been looking for you.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:46.910
-Me?
-Right.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:48.370
As Shibuya's last hope,

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:51.410
we'll restart the String Puppets

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.960
and dispatch the SDS.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.470
<i>Charge the Cube?</i>

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:03.380
<i>How?</i>

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.930
People from electric companies
and other experts checked the Cube.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:09.310
They figured out a way to charge it.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:12.100
It was possible only because
there's no power generation here.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.440
They used various methods
to store power from outside sources.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:19.070
It's all thanks to the people.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.410
Everyone here cooperated
to make this happen.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.200
<i>Little by little, we gathered ideas.</i>

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.410
<i>Instead of using power for daily living,</i>

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.580
<i>they conserved it
and bet on our last hope.</i>

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.000
Riko and Kaori too?

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.080
Little by little.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.420
That's right.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.340
All these people in Shibuya helped out.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:41.420
This is...

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.220
Everyone's wish.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:47.010
The only people
who can protect Shibuya are the SDS.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.930
Get those Revisions!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.640
You guys are our last hope!

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.460
<i>I'll infiltrate the Revisions' base alone.</i>

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.510
I know where the quantum brain is.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:28.220
Besides, either Gai or I have to stay
and defend Shibuya, right?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.390
I don't have the ability to lead everyone.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.980
I knew that from the start.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:36.690
I guess you're right.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.020
Leave Shibuya to me.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.070
We'll do this together.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.360
Right.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.690
And you're sure
about that other thing, right?

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:45.650
Yes.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.030
When set on self-destruct,

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.740
the String Puppet can be used
as a time bomb.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.370
Then you'll return with us,
right, Daisuke?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.660
You will return, right?

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.580
You can promise that, right?

00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:59.830
It will be all right, Marimari.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:01.840
This guy is stupid, you know.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.800
I mean, he's carrying our destiny
on his shoulders.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.260
-I swear he'll return.
-Okay.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.970
Why are you calling me stupid?

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.220
A smart kid can't do this.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.430
What? What are you talking about?

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.440
<i>I'm an AHRV Balancer.</i>

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.280
<i>As my role implies,
I maintain balance in the flow of time.</i>

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:27.610
<i>It's my duty to guide the future down
the best path.</i>

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:33.030
<i>I'm sure you won't be able to forgive me
for what I'm about to do.</i>

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.830
<i>So, at the very least I pray that</i>

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:41.750
<i>this choice leads to a future
that will give hope to you.</i>

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.090
<i>If we can meet again someday, then...</i>

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.230
<i>You still need more materials
to build a new body?</i>

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.400
<i>I have enough.</i>

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.150
Also, I've found out

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:05.110
that the Crystal of the Void can replace
the quantum brain.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:07.110
Then, assemble all our forces,

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.530
and give Shibuya to me as my playground.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.820
Do as you wish with it.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:14.450
Come to think of it,

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:17.500
what you said before
about escaping the shackles of time...

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:19.290
What about it?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.750
I find it hard to believe, but...

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.500
are you up to something?

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:24.920
An intruder?

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.590
There are enemies headed this way.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.760
As many as before...
No, there might be more.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.270
<i>That many?</i>

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.470
It's all right.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.600
<i>I'll deal with all of them.</i>

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.810
<i>I'm sure Daisuke will do his part too.</i>

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.780
We fight again, Nicholas!

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.110
Yes.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:53.070
-You know, you've got perfect timing.
-What?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:56.030
Nicholas is being reborn
right this moment.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.490
Who cares about that?

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.120
This is for Keisaku!

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:05.460
Daisuke, do you intend to shoot me?

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:09.340
You want to shoot me
the moment I'm reborn?

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:12.630
I have the ultimate bad luck.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:14.680
Keisaku?

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.350
Correct, but incorrect.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:21.430
Keisaku Asano is a part of me,
but not all of me.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:24.770
Can you comprehend that, poor boy?

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.440
Why, you! You're Nicholas!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.400
Why do you look like Keisaku?

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:31.780
Again, you see, he is a part of me.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.450
You just can't keep up, can you?

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.660
But you can call me Nicholas, Daisuke.

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:39.080
Goddamn you!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.790
Give Keisaku back to me!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.250
Now, now.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.460
How dare you point a gun at a friend?

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.340
Pow!

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.420
<i>Emergency!
Gravitational irregularity detected.</i>

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:52.510
<i>-It's recommended to leave immediately.</i>
-Nicholas!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.840
Why did you choose that form?

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:55.800
What's wrong with you?

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:57.970
He's the guy who killed Chiharu!

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.230
Nicholas!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:10.230
It will be all right. He will return.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.440
Yes. I believe in him.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.280
<i>Daisuke, fight for Keisaku too.</i>

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.740
Full-body exercise!

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.410
<i>It appears that Keisaku Asano
and a String Puppet were combined.</i>

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.830
<i>-Its consciousness is a complex fusion.</i>
-Can Keisaku be separated from it?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.130
<i>Impossible.</i>

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.090
<i>Not only his memories,</i>

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:32.510
<i>but also the elements of his character,</i>

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:35.630
<i>such as feelings,
in other words, what is called his soul...</i>

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:37.890
Cut it out! Quit doing that here!

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.470
Oh, sorry. My apologies.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:44.600
This is so much fun!

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.440
You're pretty good, poor boy.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:52.980
Is it your "destiny" that spurs you on?

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:53.900
No!

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:57.570
I simply want to protect everyone
and save Keisaku.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.740
That's all!

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.120
Don't make that face.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.950
You have always been too serious.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.580
If you spend every day on edge,
you'll go crazy.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.090
A nutcase!

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.130
You bastard!

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.760
I told you not to fight here!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.260
The quantum brain is here too!

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:22.050
Giant spin!

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.230
What the hell do you think...

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.660
What?

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:43.120
Nicholas? Are you...

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:47.160
Congratulations, poor boy.

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:50.210
Now that the quantum brain
doing the observation here is gone,

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.590
Shibuya will return to where it was.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.770
<i>Don't tell me
that it's returning to our time!</i>

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:38.110
Hurry up and get back here, Daisuke.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.740
No, not yet...

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:46.410
The observation isn't over yet.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:51.870
I have merged with
the Crystal of the Void,

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:55.500
so I can exist in
any time-space location simultaneously.

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.920
I have become
an ultra-high dimensional being.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:02.050
There's no point in continuing
the Revisions' plan now.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.430
Why don't you think about it this way?

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:10.890
Humanity has sacrificed itself
to give birth to me.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.810
What about Chiharu's sacrifice?

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:17.060
What about our big mission?

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:23.570
Let me tell you this before I leave.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:24.490
What?

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.990
Actually, AHRV predicted

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:29.450
that the real leader
of the String Puppet pilots

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:32.370
would be me, Keisaku Asano.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.460
What are you talking about?

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:37.040
<i>Master, Keisaku Asano was</i>

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:41.250
<i>predicted to be the most important person
before the transportation of Shibuya.</i>

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.720
<i>He was supposed to be the first person
to pilot a String Puppet.</i>

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.550
<i>Since Daisuke Dojima</i>

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.720
<i>had no distinctive abilities
out of all the pilots,</i>

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.520
<i>he was designated as a backup member.</i>

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:55.520
No abilities? A backup?

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.440
Dojima?

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.360
They're more ignorant than we expected.

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:02.610
Are you hurt, Daisuke? Daisuke!

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:04.610
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:06.450
<i>You're kidding.</i>

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:08.910
Somewhere, AHRV messed up

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:11.240
their prediction of the future.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:14.660
Then, the elimination of Keisaku is...

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:19.880
Naturally, AHRV will try
to kill Keisaku Asano

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:21.960
who is a part of me.

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:27.050
For an agent who can leap through time,
it's a piece of cake.

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:30.090
However, I won't let that happen.
I can't let it happen.

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:32.510
In fact, there's no way that can happen.

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:38.520
Goodbye, you pathetic buffoon
who thought you were the lead character.

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:41.650
This is where I say farewell, you upstart.

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:42.770
Wait, Nicholas!

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:44.820
Back off! Go away!

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.490
You have no more part in this!

00:22:50.110 --> 00:22:52.120
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
